Objects consist of changeable }{\f5\i\b0
attributes}{\f5\i0\b0
, which describe an object's properties, and }{\f5\i\b0
methods}{\f5\i0\b0
, which describe the object's behavior and how it depends on its own attributes and its interaction with other objects.  Methods are tied to }{\f5\i\b0
messages}{\f5\i0\b0
; when the object receives that message, the method associated with it is invoked.}
{\hich\af5\ai0\ab0\dbch\ai0\ab0\loch\f5\i0\b0\par}\pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af10\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar\f5\i0\b0

